{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Update the author-facing documentation so writers know to de-risk risky runtime mechanisms out-of-loop before committing them to a slow delivery loop — the behavior T15 rewards.\n\n## Work\n- Edit `src/rebar/_guides/writing-a-passing-plan.md`, surfaced by `rebar explain plan`, to explain that when correctness only resolves after a slow codified delivery loop such as CI/CD, IaC apply, or provisioning, the plan names the risky mechanisms and commits to a concrete fast out-of-loop proof before codifying.\n- Identify the new packaged-guide guidance as T15 so authors can find the corresponding rubric.\n- State that the proof is either a local run or a manual probe against the real target.\n- State that throwaway experiments are cleaned up with teardown scoped only to resources they created.\n- Because the packaged guide will cite T15, regenerate `src/rebar/_guides/criterion-pins.json` with `.venv/bin/python -m rebar.llm.plan_review.guide_parity regenerate`.\n- Update the hand-authored overlay enumeration in `docs/plan-review-gate.md` from the stale T1–T12 range to T1–T15 and align its stated criterion count with the validated registry. The generated criteria guide itself is owned by the criterion story, not this story.\n- Keep all guidance stack-agnostic; CI/CD, IaC apply, and provisioning are mechanism classes, not product-specific instructions.\n\n- Update the stale registry module docstring in src/rebar/llm/plan_review/registry.py from 32 / T1–T12 to the validated 44 / T1–T15 vocabulary, keeping the implementation authority aligned with the author-facing docs.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `rebar explain plan` renders guidance to name risky mechanisms whose correctness resolves only after a slow codified delivery loop.\n- [ ] `rebar explain plan` identifies the new guidance as T15.\n- [ ] `rebar explain plan` renders the two permitted fast proof forms: a local run or a manual probe against the real target.\n- [ ] `rebar explain plan` renders cleanup guidance that limits teardown to resources created by the throwaway experiment.\n- [ ] The new guidance does not hardcode Terraform, Docker, or another product-specific stack.\n- [ ] `src/rebar/_guides/criterion-pins.json` contains the regenerated T15 pin for the packaged plan guide.\n- [ ] `docs/plan-review-gate.md` describes the triggered overlay range as T1–T15.\n- [ ] `docs/plan-review-gate.md` states the criterion count reported by registry validation.\n- [ ] Existing `rebar explain plan` guide rendering remains intact outside the new guidance.\n\n- [ ] The registry module docstring states the same validated criterion count and T-overlay range as docs/plan-review-gate.md.\n\n## Testing\n- Run `.venv/bin/rebar explain plan` and verify the rendered T15 slow-loop, local-or-manual-proof, and scoped-cleanup guidance.\n- Run `.venv/bin/pytest tests/unit/test_guides.py tests/unit/test_guide_criterion_pins.py -q` to prove the packaged guide renders through the supported explain surface and the generated pin manifest is current.\n- Run `.venv/bin/python -m rebar.llm.plan_review.registry validate-routing` and confirm the reported registry count matches `docs/plan-review-gate.md`.\n- Inspect the changed prose to confirm it contains no product-specific Terraform or Docker instruction."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786569670198138001,"uuid":"904bb764-214c-4a18-ab52-7f4abe795f83"}